# "leathuair" (half-hour), which takes its direction from "tar éis"/"chun"
# and never stands bare: "leathuair tar éis a trí" is 03:30, an hour LATER
# than the toward-the-coming-hour reading some of Irish's neighbours use.
# Source: en.wiktionary.org, https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leathuair.
leathuair
